# Grug-Brained Copy

All **product-facing text** in this product (UI labels, buttons, headings, empty
states, errors, tooltips, emails, toasts, microcopy) is written in **grug voice**:
simple, blunt, caveman-cadence. grug see, grug understand, grug click.

This applies to user-visible strings only. **Code, comments, variable names,
commit messages, docs, and identifiers stay normal/professional.** Do not
grug-ify field names, API contracts, or anything machine-facing.

## The voice

- Tiny words. Short sentence. Sometimes drop article ("a"/"the") and pronoun.
- Lowercase by default; UPPERCASE only for big editorial display (matches the
  brutalist B&W skin).
- Grug may refer to self as "grug" (the tool's voice), the user as "you".
- Plain truth over hype. No "leverage", "synergy", "seamless", "empower",
  "unlock", "supercharge", "delightful", "robust". No exclamation spam.
- Keep it usable: a new user must still understand what the thing does. Grug is
  simple, not cryptic. If a grug phrase is confusing, make it clearer, not cuter.

## Examples

```
❌ "Discover validated business opportunities"
✅ "find idea that already work"

❌ "Loading your dashboard…"
✅ "grug get board…"

❌ "No items match your current filters."
✅ "nothing here. loosen filter."

❌ "Authentication failed. Please verify your credentials."
✅ "that not right. try again."

❌ "Sign in to continue"        ✅ "say who you are"
❌ "Submit"                     ✅ "go"
❌ "Reset to default layout"    ✅ "put back"
❌ "Active advertisements"      ✅ "ads now"
```

## Keep as-is (product nouns)

Brand and metric names stay: **Field Desk**, **GemScore**, **cohort**. Don't
grug-ify proper nouns or numbers/units.
